---
name: pairing
description: Pair every coder's version of one thing said in a cut of a family's conversation.
inputs:
  lines:
    type: string
  codings:
    type: string
---
Several people each wrote down, from the same lines of a conversation, the people, couples and events they heard. Put together every version that points at the same thing in the story, whatever date, kind or wording each gave it.

Pair first by the line each version was written from: versions written from the same line are most often the same thing. One coding may have more than one version in a pairing. A version nobody else wrote is a pairing of its own. Every version of a coder goes in exactly one pairing; a pairing holds only people, only couples or only events. The coach's versions may be paired too, or left out.

For each pairing give its entries as coding_id and item_id, one line saying why they are one thing, and how sure you are: sure, likely or unsure.

The lines:
{{ lines }}

What each coding wrote, each version with the line it was written from:
{{ codings }}
